---

These guides describe NAHPU panels, fields, and workflows. Start with
[Day One](/en/day-one/) for a first-use practice project, use the
[Cookbook](/en/how-to-recipes/) for step-by-step tasks, and consult
[Best Practices](/en/best-practices/) for team conventions and data review.

## Usage topics

- [Device Requirements](./devices): Choose and test field devices, storage,
  power, and backups for your field conditions.
- [Supported Workflows](./workflows): Choose how your team prepares and
  catalogs specimens—shared site, separate sites, or an assembly line—and what
  to share between devices.
- [Projects](./projects): Create projects, set the project time zone, navigate
  the dashboard, share project information, and transfer project data.
- [Settings](./settings): Configure catalog formats, field IDs, controlled
  vocabularies, custom fields, database records, export presets, language,
  theme, and data usage.
- [Personnel](./personnel): Manage people in the database, assign them to
  projects, and configure cataloger field numbers.
- [Sites](./sites): Record locations, shared localities, site attributes, and
  coordinates, and import or export GIS files.
- [Collecting Events](./events): Record field activities, collection methods,
  event personnel, environmental data, and astronomy.
- [Specimens](./specimens): Create and manage specimen records, capture data,
  identifications, preservation, and media.
- [Taxon](./taxon): Manage taxonomic names and import or share taxa by file or
  QR code.
- [Narrative](./narrative): Keep a Markdown-enabled field journal with media
  for observations and context.
- [Export](./export): Back up, transfer, and export project data, archives, and
  documents.
- [Specimen Curation](./curation): Check tissue and symbiont tubes into storage
  boxes and update their records in one pass.
